Scenario: Validate Reg Ex Password Policy CP
Priority: 4
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	When User add CP
		|userEmailAddress|test1@liferay.com|
		|userFirstName|test1|
		|userLastName|test1|
		|userScreenName|test1|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Password Policies|
	And Click at locator 'PasswordPolicies#DEFAULT_PASSWORD_POLICY_TABLE_ACTIONS_BUTTON'
	And AssertClick the value 'Edit' at locator 'MenuItem#EDIT'
	And Panel expand Panel
		|panelHeading|Password Syntax Checking|
	And Check check Toggle Switch at locator 'Checkbox#ENABLE_SYNTAX_CHECKING'
	And Uncheck uncheck Toggle Switch at locator 'Checkbox#ALLOW_DICTIONARY_WORDS'
	And Type the value '0' at locator 'TextInput#MINIMUM_ALPHA_NUMERIC'
	And Type the value '0' at locator 'TextInput#MINIMUM_LENGTH'
	And Type the value '0' at locator 'TextInput#MINIMUM_LOWER_CASE'
	And Type the value '0' at locator 'TextInput#MINIMUM_NUMBERS'
	And Type the value '0' at locator 'TextInput#MINIMUM_SYMBOLS'
	And Type the value '0' at locator 'TextInput#MINIMUM_UPPER_CASE'
	And Type the value '(?=.{4})(?:[a-zA-Z]*)' at locator 'TextInput#REGULAR_EXPRESSION'
	And Button click Save
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User edit Password Invalid CP
		|newPassword|NO1else|
		|regex|(?=.{4})(?:[a-zA-Z]*)|
		|userEmailAddress|test1@liferay.com|
		|userScreenName|test1|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User edit Password CP
		|newPassword|tryingHARD|
		|resetPassword|tryingHARDER|
		|syntaxCheckingEnabled|true|
		|userEmailAddress|test1@liferay.com|
		|userScreenName|test1|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Password Policies|
	And Click at locator 'PasswordPolicies#DEFAULT_PASSWORD_POLICY_TABLE_ACTIONS_BUTTON'
	And AssertClick the value 'Edit' at locator 'MenuItem#EDIT'
	And Panel expand Panel
		|panelHeading|Password Syntax Checking|
	And Type the value '(?=.{6})(?:[a-zA-Z0-9]*)' at locator 'TextInput#REGULAR_EXPRESSION'
	And Button click Save
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User edit Password CP
		|newPassword|abcABC|
		|resetPassword|abcdABCD|
		|syntaxCheckingEnabled|true|
		|userEmailAddress|test1@liferay.com|
